{
  "_name": "test_freq_mismatch",
  "_desc": "FREQUENCY-SELECTIVE PHY gate (§carrier, 2026-07-26 owner ruling). Three isolated groups over one fixture. GROUP A: one 868 MHz sender; receivers on the INHERITED carrier / a far carrier / an ADJACENT 868.1 MHz carrier (hard split, no adjacent-channel leniency) / retuned both ways / off-net at both carriers. GROUP B: LBT orthogonality — a same-carrier neighbour IS deferred, a cross-carrier one is NOT. GROUP C: hidden-terminal collision — same-carrier frames destroy each other, cross-carrier frames do not. Analytically deterministic: no fading (snr_std_dev 0), no PER sigmoid (steepness 0), no preamble miss, no startup jitter, no warmup (warmup bypasses ALL physics gates by contract, carrier included). ★ simulation.radio.freq_khz is DELIBERATELY ABSENT so the run also proves the 868000 default AND the per-node inherit. ★ Runs on the DEPRECATED Lua engine BY NECESSITY (build_test.sh cannot link FirmwareNode) — hence the explicit per-node \"engine\":\"lua\" plus allow_deprecated_lua: the sanctioned internal use that opt-in exists for.",
